  "_comment": "Character names for Realm Invader Episode 2 Part 2, read out of the _realm_invader_name_replacements table in patch/tl/schinese/characters.rpy so the two cannot drift. This game has no name table in its shim -- unlike Por(n)tals, whose shim owns ZH_CHARACTER_NAMES -- because the developer already shipped the replacement tuple inside the translation file itself, where Ren'Py applies it to every speaker name. Nothing is listed as banned: check.py matches banned forms as plain substrings, and most of these names are also ordinary Chinese words (孩子, 学生, 老师, 陌生人, 安保人员), which would make a ban fire on correct prose.",
  "_kept_verbatim": [
    "DejaVu Sans",
    "Opendyslexic",
    "a",
    "q",
    "★.",
    "♥♥♥",
    "♥♥♥♥♥♥♥"
  ],
  "_why_kept_verbatim": "Seven entries, all of which reading as English (or as no language at all) is correct. 'DejaVu Sans' and 'Opendyslexic' are font family names printed in the font-picker and credits screens; translating a typeface's name would break every other tool that looks it up. 'a' and 'q' are single keystrokes in the key-binding and quick-save prompts, where the surrounding sentence already carries the meaning. '★.', '♥♥♥' and '♥♥♥♥♥♥♥' are decorative filler made of symbols and no letters: the player reads the rhythm, not words, so there is nothing to translate.",
